[["text","LESSON 04 / 31 • ORIGINAL CHECKLIST"],["heading","4. Stacks"],["text","English: A last-in, first-out (LIFO) collection."],["sinhala","","සිංහල: අන්තිමට දාපු item එක මුලින්ම ඉවෙත් Jවෙනවො.",281],["text","Real-world example: Undo actions"],["code","TOP -> [20]"],["code","       [10]"],["heading","Java example / illustration"],["code","Deque<Integer> s = new ArrayDeque<>();\ns.push(10); s.push(20);\nSystem.out.println(s.pop()); // 20"],["heading","Complexity and trade-offs"],["text","Push/pop/peek amortized O(1) with ArrayDeque."],["heading","Interview question"],["heading","What is LIFO?"],["text","Last in, first out."],["heading","Quick practice"],["text","Explain this concept aloud, trace the example, and describe when you would choose this"],["text","structure over an alternative."]]